{
  "id": "COMPOUND:10898 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Tucaresol is implicated in the targeting of multiple molecular entities, including the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. These targets are in turn linked to Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, suggesting a potential pathway where Tucaresol influences the activity of these proteins, which in turn modulate the kinase activity of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The evidence is consistent across three paths, with Tucaresol acting as a common intermediary that leads to the activation or regulation of the kinase through different molecular targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Tucaresol in modulating the kinase activity through a series of interconnected molecular targets, emphasizing the complex network of interactions that may underlie its biological effects.",
